---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../components/PageHero.astro';
import CTABand from '../components/CTABand.astro';

// PackForge, the report product, runs as its own application at
// reports.salet.uk. It shares the engine behind the free tools on this site,
// so a visitor who has used the price check meets the same discipline here.
const REPORTS_URL = 'https://reports.salet.uk';
---
<Base
  title="Property reports | Legal pack review | Salet"
  description="Upload an auction pack, a lease or a management pack and get back what the documents actually say, with the document and page behind every finding. Free while we launch."
>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Reports"
    title="Read the pack before you bid"
    lede="An auction legal pack is where the cost hides. We read it against a named risk checklist and report what it says, with the page behind every finding. What the pack does not answer is reported too, with the question to send your solicitor."
    compact
  />

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-6 py-16 lg:px-8 lg:py-24">
    <div class="grid gap-14 lg:grid-cols-12">
      <div class="lg:col-span-7">
        <h2 class="reveal font-display text-3xl font-medium tracking-tight text-ink">
          Legal Pack Review
        </h2>
        <p class="reveal mt-5 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate">
          Upload the pack. Every finding comes back with the document and the page number it rests
          on, graded by whether it changes the price, needs an answer before exchange, or is simply
          worth knowing.
        </p>
        <p class="reveal mt-4 text-lg leading-relaxed text-slate">
          The part most reviews skip is the part that costs money: what the pack leaves out. Missing
          searches, absent service charge accounts and unanswered title questions are reported as
          gaps, each with the question to put to the solicitor or the auctioneer.
        </p>

        <ul class="reveal mt-8 space-y-3 text-base text-slate">
          <li class="border-l-2 border-green-2 pl-4">
            Special conditions read clause by clause, because that is where costs move to the buyer.
          </li>
          <li class="border-l-2 border-green-2 pl-4">
            Ground rent, lease term, service charge arrears and s20 notices, quoted with their figures.
          </li>
          <li class="border-l-2 border-green-2 pl-4">
            Tenancies, covenants, searches and the full fee stack on top of the hammer price.
          </li>
        </ul>

        <a
          href={REPORTS_URL}
          class="reveal mt-10 inline-block bg-[#c2410c] px-7 py-4 text-base font-medium text-ivory transition-colors hover:bg-[#a33608]"
        >
          Upload a legal pack
        </a>
        <p class="reveal mt-4 text-xs leading-relaxed text-mist">
          Free while we launch. Your documents are deleted 90 days after the report completes, and
          you can delete them yourself at any time. The review states what the documents say. It is
          not legal advice, and a solicitor must review the pack before exchange.
        </p>
      </div>

      <aside class="lg:col-span-5">
        <div class="reveal border border-line bg-ivory p-8">
          <h3 class="font-display text-xl font-medium tracking-tight text-ink">
            Already used the free tools?
          </h3>
          <p class="mt-4 text-base leading-relaxed text-slate">
            The report runs on the same engine as the three free checks on this site. If the numbers
            stack up and you are heading for the auction room, the pack is the next thing to read.
          </p>
          <div class="mt-6 space-y-3 text-base">
            <a href="/deal-check" class="block text-green-2 underline">What should I offer?</a>
            <a href="/price-check" class="block text-green-2 underline">House price estimate</a>
            <a href="/refurb-check" class="block text-green-2 underline">Refurbishment calculator</a>
          </div>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </section>

  <CTABand />
</Base>
